import{_ as e,c as o,o as i,a3 as d}from"./chunks/framework.Bsyxd66g.js";const b=JSON.parse('{"title":"Bilibili client","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"subsystems/bilibili-client.md","filePath":"subsystems/bilibili-client.md","lastUpdated":1794660158000}'),c={name:"subsystems/bilibili-client.md"},t=d('<h1 id="bilibili-client" tabindex="-1">Bilibili client <a class="header-anchor" href="#bilibili-client" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Bilibili client&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="responsibility-and-boundaries" tabindex="-1">Responsibility and boundaries <a class="header-anchor" href="#responsibility-and-boundaries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Responsibility and boundaries&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Owns: every outbound request to Bilibili — endpoint paths and query parameters, WBI signing, cookie/credential handling and refresh, response-envelope validation, error classification (risk control, invalid status, empty streams), rate limiting and shared HTTP client construction; parsing of source lists, video details, pages, tags, play URLs, subtitles and danmaku segments.</li><li>Does not own: when requests are issued and what is done with the results (<a href="./sync-pipeline">sync-pipeline.md</a>); local file layout (<a href="./media-artifacts">media-artifacts.md</a>); where the credential is stored (<a href="./config-and-persistence">config-and-persistence.md</a>).</li><li>Talks to: <code>VersionedConfig</code>/<code>VersionedCache</code> for credentials and rate limits, <code>reqwest</code> for transport, <code>sea-orm</code> only indirectly through <code>utils::convert</code> models returned to the pipeline, and <code>crate::downloader</code> for byte transfer of already-resolved stream URLs.</li></ul><h2 id="sources-of-truth" tabindex="-1">Sources of truth <a class="header-anchor" href="#sources-of-truth" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Sources of truth&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Authoritative HTTP behavior: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/bilibili/client.rs</code> (client, limiter, snapshot, <code>request</code>) and <code>crates/bili_sync/src/bilibili/mod.rs</code> (<code>Validate</code>, <code>WbiSign</code>, <code>ErrorForStatusExt</code>, <code>MIXIN_KEY</code>).</li><li>Authoritative error taxonomy: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/bilibili/error.rs</code> (<code>BiliError</code>, <code>is_risk_control_related</code>, <code>is_common_error</code>). Nothing else may decide what &quot;risk control&quot; means.</li><li>Authoritative endpoint list: the per-area modules under <code>crates/bili_sync/src/bilibili/</code> — <code>video.rs</code>, <code>favorite_list.rs</code>, <code>collection.rs</code>, <code>submission.rs</code>, <code>watch_later.rs</code>, <code>dynamic.rs</code>, <code>me.rs</code>, <code>credential.rs</code>. There is no endpoint registry elsewhere.</li><li>Authoritative stream selection: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/bilibili/analyzer.rs</code> (<code>FilterOption</code>, <code>Stream</code>, <code>BestStream</code>, <code>PageAnalyzer::{streams,best_stream}</code>, <code>Stream::urls</code>).</li><li>Forbidden duplicate sources: re-signing or re-validating responses in the pipeline, hard-coded duplicate endpoint URLs in other modules, or building ad-hoc <code>reqwest::Client</code> instances for Bilibili calls.</li></ul><h2 id="main-paths-change-loci" tabindex="-1">Main paths / change loci <a class="header-anchor" href="#main-paths-change-loci" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Main paths / change loci&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Key entry points: <ul><li><code>crates/bili_sync/src/bilibili/client.rs</code> (<code>Client::new</code>, <code>BiliClient::new</code>, <code>BiliClient::snapshot</code>, <code>BiliClient::request</code>, <code>BiliClient::wbi_img</code>, <code>BiliClient::check_refresh</code>).</li><li><code>crates/bili_sync/src/bilibili/mod.rs</code> (<code>set_global_mixin_key</code>, <code>Validate::validate</code>, <code>WbiSign::wbi_sign</code>).</li><li><code>crates/bili_sync/src/bilibili/credential.rs</code> (<code>Credential::{generate_qrcode,poll_qrcode,need_refresh,refresh,extract}</code>).</li></ul></li><li>Common edit locations: <ul><li>New endpoint: add a method to the matching module and reuse <code>self.client.get(...).wbi_sign()...validate().await</code>; add any new envelope/field types in the same module.</li><li>New error condition: <code>error.rs</code> variants plus <code>is_risk_control_related</code>/<code>is_common_error</code>, then callers in <code>workflow.rs</code> only if semantics change.</li><li>Quality/codec/audio preferences: <code>FilterOption</code> defaults and <code>PageAnalyzer::streams</code>/<code>best_stream</code> in <code>analyzer.rs</code>.</li><li>Danmaku appearance: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/bilibili/danmaku/mod.rs</code> (<code>DanmakuOption</code>), rendering in <code>canvas.rs</code>/<code>ass_writer.rs</code>.</li><li>Rate limiting shape: <code>ConcurrentLimit::rate_limit</code> in <code>crates/bili_sync/src/config/item.rs</code> and <code>Limiter</code> in <code>client.rs</code>.</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="runtime-paths-and-state-transitions" tabindex="-1">Runtime paths and state transitions <a class="header-anchor" href="#runtime-paths-and-state-transitions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Runtime paths and state transitions&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Trigger / inputs / outputs / interfaces: <ul><li>Inputs: a <code>BiliClient</code> (limiter mode <code>Latest(VersionedCache)</code> for live config or <code>Snapshot</code> for a frozen run), the current <code>Credential</code>, the global WBI mixin key, and call-specific parameters (fid, sid, mid, bvid, cid, pn, keyword).</li><li>Outputs: typed JSON models (<code>VideoInfo</code>, <code>PageAnalyzer</code>, <code>PageInfo</code>, tag lists, <code>SubTitle</code>, danmaku segments) or a <code>BiliError</code>.</li><li>Interface contract: <code>Client</code> sends <code>Cookie: buvid3=…; SESSDATA=…; bili_jct=…; DedeUserID=…</code>, a desktop Chrome <code>User-Agent</code>, and <code>Referer: https://www.bilibili.com/</code>; it enables gzip and uses 10-second connect and read timeouts.</li></ul></li><li>Main execution path (source files and named symbols): <ol><li>Every call funnels through <code>BiliClient::request</code>, which awaits the <code>leaky_bucket</code> limiter built from <code>ConcurrentLimit::rate_limit</code> (default <code>4</code> permits per <code>250 ms</code>, <code>None</code> disables it) and then issues the request with the shared <code>reqwest::Client</code>.</li><li>Requests needing WBI signing call <code>.wbi_sign()</code> (<code>WbiSign</code>), which sorts all form/query fields, appends <code>wts</code> (unix seconds) and <code>w_rid</code> (md5 of the query string salted with the mixin key from <code>MIXIN_KEY: ArcSwapOption&lt;String&gt;</code>).</li><li><code>.validate::&lt;T&gt;()</code> deserializes the JSON envelope <code>{ code, message, data }</code>: <ul><li>missing <code>code</code> → <code>BiliError::InvalidResponse</code>;</li><li><code>code == -352</code> or a non-null <code>data.v_voucher</code> → <code>BiliError::RiskControlOccurred</code>;</li><li>any other non-zero <code>code</code> → <code>BiliError::ErrorResponse { code, message, response }</code>.</li></ul></li><li><code>ErrorForStatusExt</code> turns HTTP <code>412</code> and <code>403</code> responses into <code>BiliError::InvalidStatusCode(status, reason)</code>, where <code>reason</code> is the HTTP status&#39;s canonical reason phrase before body validation.</li><li>Source enumeration: <code>favorite_list.rs</code> (<code>/x/v3/fav/folder/info</code>, <code>/x/v3/fav/resource/list</code>), <code>collection.rs</code> (<code>/x/series/series</code>, <code>/x/series/archives</code>, <code>/x/polymer/web-space/seasons_archives_list</code>), <code>submission.rs</code> (<code>/x/web-interface/card</code>, <code>/x/space/wbi/arc/search</code>), <code>watch_later.rs</code> (<code>/x/v2/history/toview</code>), <code>dynamic.rs</code> (<code>/x/polymer/web-dynamic/v1/feed/space</code>). Each module&#39;s <code>VideoInfo</code> variant maps into <code>utils::convert</code> models where validity and time fields are decided.</li><li>Details and media: <code>video.rs</code> <code>get_view_info</code> (<code>/x/web-interface/wbi/view</code>), <code>get_tags</code> (<code>/x/web-interface/view/detail/tag</code>), <code>get_page_analyzer</code> (<code>/x/player/wbi/playurl</code>, <code>qn=127</code>/<code>fnval=4048</code>/<code>fourk=1</code> → <code>PageAnalyzer</code>), <code>get_subtitles</code> (<code>/x/player/wbi/v2</code>, then downloads each subtitle URL with <code>https:</code> prefixed when the URL is protocol-relative), <code>get_danmaku_writer</code> (<code>duration.div_ceil(360)</code> segments from <code>/x/v2/dm/wbi/web/seg.so?type=1</code>, protobuf <code>DmSegMobileReply</code>, requires <code>content-type: application/octet-stream</code>, segments sorted by progress).</li><li>Account data: <code>me.rs</code> <code>get_created_favorites</code>, <code>get_followed_collections</code>, <code>get_followed_uppers</code>; each starts with <code>ensure!(!self.mid().is_empty(), &quot;未获取到用户 ID，请确保填写设置中的 B 站认证信息&quot;)</code>.</li></ol></li><li>State ownership, transitions and persistence: <ul><li><code>MIXIN_KEY</code> is process-global and replaced once per download round by <code>set_global_mixin_key</code>; it is not persisted.</li><li><code>Credential</code> is the only persisted auth state and is owned by <code>VersionedConfig</code>; <code>refresh</code> mutates it through <code>update_credential</code>, which also bumps the config version so the front-end reloads.</li><li>Credential refresh sequence: <code>need_refresh</code> (expired cookie or <code>data.refresh</code> in <code>/x/web-interface/nav</code>) → <code>refresh</code> requests <code>https://www.bilibili.com/correspond/1/{correspond_path}</code> (RSA-OAEP SHA-256 with <code>ts = now - 20000 ms</code>) to extract <code>refresh_csrf</code> → <code>/x/passport-login/web/cookie/refresh</code> with <code>csrf</code>/<code>refresh_csrf</code>/<code>refresh_token</code>/<code>source=main_web</code> → <code>/x/passport-login/web/confirm/refresh</code>; <code>extract</code> requires <code>SESSDATA</code>, <code>bili_jct</code> and <code>DedeUserID</code> from <code>Set-Cookie</code> plus a <code>refresh_token</code>.</li><li>QR login is stateless: <code>generate_qrcode</code> returns the QR URL and key; <code>poll_qrcode</code> maps API codes <code>0</code> → success (credential extracted), <code>86101</code> → pending, unscanned, <code>86090</code> → pending, scanned, <code>86038</code> → expired.</li><li>Per-run snapshots: <code>BiliClient::snapshot()</code> freezes the current limiter/config so a config edit mid-run cannot change behavior; calling <code>snapshot()</code> on an already-snapshot client is an error (<code>cannot snapshot a snapshot BiliClient</code>).</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="constraints-and-failures" tabindex="-1">Constraints and failures <a class="header-anchor" href="#constraints-and-failures" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Constraints and failures&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Invariants: <ul><li>No Bilibili request may bypass <code>BiliClient::request</code> (rate limiter) and <code>.validate::&lt;T&gt;()</code> (envelope checks).</li><li>WBI-signed endpoints must sign the exact final query string; adding a query parameter after signing silently breaks the request.</li><li><code>BiliError::RiskControlOccurred</code>, <code>VideoStreamsEmpty</code> and <code>InvalidStatusCode</code> are the only risk-control signals (<code>is_risk_control_related</code>); do not add new classes without updating that predicate and <a href="./sync-pipeline">sync-pipeline.md</a>.</li><li><code>BiliError::is_common_error</code> recognizes only <code>-503 服务暂不可用</code> and <code>-504 服务调用超时</code>; those are suppressed when <code>Config::ignore_common_errors</code> is enabled.</li></ul></li><li>Failure modes and recovery: <ul><li>Risk control → stream is cut and the round stops (see the pipeline page); the client itself never retries.</li><li><code>VideoStreamsEmpty</code> when <code>/dash/video</code> is absent; usually geo/paid/charging content. It is treated as risk control, not as a per-video failure.</li><li><code>InvalidStatusCode(412|403)</code> frequently accompanies risk control; the same handling applies.</li><li><code>-404</code> on <code>get_view_info</code> is surfaced as <code>ErrorResponse { code: -404 }</code> and the pipeline marks the video invalid rather than failing the round.</li><li>Credential refresh failures are logged and notified through <code>check_and_refresh_credential_task</code>; the program continues with the old credential.</li><li>Transient network/timeout/decode errors are converted to <code>ExecutionStatus::Ignored</code> by <code>crates/bili_sync/src/error.rs</code>, so they do not consume retry attempts.</li></ul></li><li>Compatibility / migration behavior: <ul><li>Bilibili changes endpoints and envelope shapes without notice; new fields should be <code>Option</code>/<code>#[serde(default)]</code> so a missing field does not fail an entire scan.</li><li><code>Credential</code> field names are the persisted JSON keys; renaming them breaks existing databases and requires a migration hook in <code>VersionedConfig</code>.</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="forbidden-patterns-and-common-mistakes" tabindex="-1">Forbidden patterns and common mistakes <a class="header-anchor" href="#forbidden-patterns-and-common-mistakes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Forbidden patterns and common mistakes&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Forbidden: creating a second <code>reqwest::Client</code> for Bilibili traffic; it would bypass the shared cookie jar and timeouts.</li><li>Forbidden: catching <code>BiliError</code> and mapping risk control to a generic failure; the pipeline depends on the distinct variant to stop the round.</li><li>Forbidden: putting retry loops inside client methods; retries are modeled by subtask counters in the pipeline.</li><li>Common mistake: assuming <code>is_upower_exclusive == is_upower_play</code> is the only validity rule. <code>utils::convert</code> combines <code>state == 0</code>, that upower equality (unless <code>try_upower_anyway</code>), and <code>redirect_url.is_none()</code>; each source kind has its own extra rule (for example favorite <code>attr</code> <code>0|4</code>, watch later <code>state == 0</code>).</li><li>Common mistake: assuming <code>get_pages</code> is used in production. It is <code>#[cfg(test)]</code>-only; the pipeline derives pages from <code>get_view_info</code>.</li><li>Common mistake: treating a subtitle URL as absolute. Subtitles may be protocol-relative and are prefixed with <code>https:</code> before download; AI subtitles (URL containing <code>ai_subtitle</code>) are filtered out.</li><li>Common mistake: expecting one danmaku request per video. Danmaku is requested per 6-minute segment (<code>duration.div_ceil(360)</code>) and only when the response declares <code>application/octet-stream</code>.</li><li>Common mistake: expecting every notifier-visible failure to be retried; <code>ExecutionStatus::Ignored</code> and <code>ignore_common_errors</code> both short-circuit.</li><li>Common mistake: assuming stream choice is &quot;best quality wins&quot;. <code>FilterOption</code> bounds video quality (<code>video_min_quality</code>/<code>video_max_quality</code>), audio quality (<code>audio_min_quality</code>/<code>audio_max_quality</code>), the allowed <code>codecs</code> list, and has <code>no_hdr</code>, <code>no_dolby_video</code>, <code>no_dolby_audio</code>, <code>no_hires</code> switches; <code>best_stream</code> then picks among the survivors in <code>analyzer.rs</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="how-to-verify" tabindex="-1">How to verify <a class="header-anchor" href="#how-to-verify" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How to verify&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Compile-level check that no direct <code>reqwest</code> usage escaped: <code>cargo clippy -p bili_sync -- -D warnings</code> (unused/duplicate client code tends to surface as warnings here).</li><li>Unit tests: <code>cargo test -p bili_sync bilibili</code> runs non-ignored tests matching <code>bilibili</code>. <code>test_video_info_type</code>, <code>test_subtitle_parse</code>, <code>test_upower_parse</code>, <code>test_ep_parse</code>, <code>test_best_stream</code> and <code>test_qrcode_login_flow</code> are ignored manual tests; run them individually with <code>cargo test -p bili_sync &lt;test_name&gt; -- --ignored</code> only when their network and credential prerequisites are available.</li><li>Manual check with a real credential: <code>POST /api/login/qrcode/generate</code> then <code>GET /api/login/qrcode/poll</code> through the running server, and confirm <code>Config.credential</code> fields change in the database (<code>config</code> row id <code>1</code>).</li><li>Manual risk-control check: run a full sync while rate-limited; the logs must show <code>检测到风控，终止此轮视频下载任务..</code> and no subtask counter increments for the aborted videos.</li><li>Manual stream-selection check: set an unusual <code>filter_option</code> (for example <code>video_max_quality</code> below 8K, or drop <code>AV1</code> from <code>codecs</code>) and confirm the downloaded file corresponds to <code>best_stream</code> (<code>Mixed</code> for flv/html5/episode-try, otherwise <code>VideoAudio</code>).</li></ul>',15),r=[t];function s(a,n,l,u,h,m){return i(),o("div",null,r)}const f=e(c,[["render",s]]);export{b as __pageData,f as default};
